  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "The q-analogue of the wild fundamental group — We describe an explicit construction of galoisian Stokes operators for irregular linear q-difference equations.\n\n**The q-analogue of the wild fundamental group**\n\n*J.-P. Ramis∗, J. Sauloy †*\n\n22 pp, 9 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We describe an explicit construction of galoisian Stokes operators for irregular linear q-difference equations. These operators are parameterized by the points of an elliptic curve minus a ﬁnite set of singularities. Taking residues at these singularities, one gets q-analogues of alien derivations which freely generate the Lie algebra of the Stokes subgroup of the Galois group.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2.1 General facts; 2.2 Filtration by the slopes; 2.3 Stokes operators; 3 Stokes operators and alien derivations; 3.1 Stokes operators are galois; 3.2 Alien derivations and $q$-Borel transform; 4 Conclusion",
      "lang": "en",
      "state": "draft",
      "drafted_by": {
        "kind": "script",
        "id": "scripts/summarize-library.py"
      },
      "drafted_at": "2026-11-24"
    }
